    "body": "TxGraph::Trim() builds a rudimentary linearization of the would-be cluster to\ndecide which transactions to remove. For the dependencies inside each involved\ncluster, it did not use the real ones: it added an implicit dependency between\neach pair of consecutive transactions in that cluster's linearization. This\nmakes transactions look dependent when they are not, which can merge\npartitions unnecessarily and cause Trim() to remove more transactions than\nneeded (see #36656).\n\nThis PR makes GenericClusterImpl::AppendTrimData() emit the cluster's actual\ndependencies (only the reduced parents, since the rest follow by transitivity)\ninstead of the implicit chain. As a result, several transactions from the same\ncluster can be in the heap at the same time. Topological order is still\nrespected, because a transaction only becomes eligible once all of its\ndependencies are met. The related comments in Trim() and in the fuzz test were\nupdated.\n\nTests:\n- New unit tests `txgraph_trim_no_cascade` and `txgraph_trim_no_overcount` in\n  src/test/txgraph_tests.cpp, based on the existing zigzag/flower Trim tests.\n- The existing `txgraph` fuzz target exercises Trim() and checks its invariants.\n\nAs noted by instagibbs in the issue, this is low priority since Trim() only\nruns during reorgs. I have not yet built or run the tests locally, so I'm\nopening this as a draft to let CI run.\n\nFixes #36656.",
